---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const title = "Terms & Conditions | ROAM SOCIAL";
const description =
  "Terms and Conditions for booking ROAM SOCIAL mobile bar services in Bengaluru — services, FSSAI compliance, alcohol policy, bookings and governing law.";
---

<LegalLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>

  <h2>1. Agreement to Terms</h2>
  <p>
    By accessing our website and booking the services of Roam Social, you agree to be bound by these
    Terms and Conditions. Please read them carefully before finalizing any event bookings.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Services Provided</h2>
  <p>Roam Social is a premium mobile beverage and catering business. We provide the following
  services for various events:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Crafted Drinks</li>
    <li>Pop-ups</li>
    <li>Private Parties</li>
    <li>Corporate Events</li>
    <li>Weddings</li>
    <li>Beverage Catering</li>
    <li>Social Bites</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. FSSAI Compliance and Safety Standard</h2>
  <p>
    Roam Social is a fully registered and compliant food business operator holding a valid FSSAI
    (Food Safety and Standards Authority of India) License. We adhere to strict hygiene, handling,
    and food safety protocols to ensure the highest quality of service for all crafted drinks and
    Social Bites.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Alcohol Policy and Client Responsibilities (Strictly Enforced)</h2>
  <p>To ensure full legal compliance and the safety of Roam Social, the following alcohol policy
  applies to all events:</p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 font-display text-lg text-white">Permits and Licensing</h3>
  <p>
    Roam Social does not sell alcohol. If alcoholic beverages are to be served at an event, the
    client is solely responsible for obtaining all necessary liquor licenses, one-day event permits,
    and venue permissions required by local state laws and excise departments.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 font-display text-lg text-white">Procurement</h3>
  <p>
    The client must procure and provide the alcohol. Roam Social acts solely as a mixing and
    bartending service for the client's provided inventory.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 font-display text-lg text-white">Liability</h3>
  <p>
    Roam Social assumes no liability for underage drinking, overconsumption, or any legal penalties
    resulting from the client's failure to secure the proper alcohol permits for their venue. We
    reserve the right to refuse service to any guest who appears severely intoxicated or unable to
    provide proof of legal drinking age.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Booking, Communication, and Logistics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All initial enquiries are processed through our website contact form.</li>
    <li>
      Final service agreements, including guest counts and specific beverage menus, must be
      confirmed prior to the event date as outlined in your specific booking invoice.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Subsequent event coordination, menu finalisation, and booking confirmations will be conducted
    strictly via email (<a href="mailto:support@roamsocial.in">support@roamsocial.in</a>) and
    WhatsApp.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
  <p>
    While we strive to provide flawless service, Roam Social shall not be held liable for any
    indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from event cancellations due to severe
    weather, acts of God, or the client's failure to secure necessary event permits (including
    alcohol licenses).
  </p>

  <h2>7. Governing Law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms and conditions are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India.
    Any disputes relating to these terms and conditions will be subject to the exclusive
    jurisdiction of the courts of India.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Cancellation and Refund Policy</h2>

  <h3 class="mt-6 font-display text-lg text-white">Booking Security and Advance Payment</h3>
  <p>
    To secure Roam Social&rsquo;s services for a specific event date, a non-refundable advance
    payment (booking fee) is required at the time of invoice acceptance. Until this advance is
    received, the date remains open for other bookings.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 font-display text-lg text-white">Non-Refundable Advance</h3>
  <p>
    The advance payment is strictly non-refundable. This policy is in place because securing your
    event date requires us to turn away other potential clients for that same time slot, and covers
    the initial administrative, logistical, and procurement efforts required to prepare for your
    event.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 font-display text-lg text-white">Cancellation by the Client</h3>
  <p>
    If you must cancel your event, you must notify us immediately via email
    (<a href="mailto:support@roamsocial.in">support@roamsocial.in</a>).
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Cancellations made after the advance has been paid will result in the forfeiture of the entire advance amount.</li>
    <li>
      Cancellations made within 7 days of the scheduled event date will require full payment of the
      remaining invoice balance, as perishable goods, staffing, and event logistics have already
      been finalized and committed to by Roam Social.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="mt-6 font-display text-lg text-white">Rescheduling</h3>
  <p>
    If you need to postpone your event, we will make every effort to accommodate the new date,
    subject to our availability. The non-refundable advance may be transferred to the new date
    provided the request is made at least 14 days prior to the original event date. If we are
    unavailable on your new date, it will be treated as a cancellation from the client&rsquo;s end.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 font-display text-lg text-white">Cancellation by Roam Social</h3>
  <p>
    In the highly unlikely event that Roam Social must cancel our services due to unforeseen
    circumstances, emergencies, or force majeure, you will receive a 100% full refund of all
    payments made to us, including the advance.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>

<style>
  .legal-body :global(h3) {
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
